      "description": "The target audience is individuals who hold racist, xenophobic, or anti-immigrant views, particularly those who believe in harmful stereotypes associating Black people and immigrants with criminality and illegality. The meme is designed to appeal to those who support or are influenced by anti-Latino/Hispanic stereotypes, immigration status assumptions, and criminality associations, as it uses the image of a Black woman to reinforce these prejudiced narratives. The audience is likely to be drawn to the meme’s hateful intent by its implication that the woman is complicit in facilitating illegal immigration, which aligns with existing biases against immigrants and people of color.",
